WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:02.939
- I can't believe it either.

00:00:02.939 --> 00:00:03.978
- [Vintage Voiceover] Well,
I have a wonderful electronic

00:00:03.978 --> 00:00:05.968
invention I want you to see.

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:07.950
It looks something like this.

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:09.093
(warp sound)

00:00:09.093 --> 00:00:10.940
- This probably isn't what
you thought DJI was going

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.810
to be launching next, did you?

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:15.280
'Cause I sure didn't but
I'm so glad they did.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.080
They're calling this an educational robot.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:20.160
This is the DJI RoboMaster S1.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.830
Since 2015, China has been
having this competition.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.400
It's called the RoboMaster Competition

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.750
and I had not heard of this
until DJI announced this.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:30.090
So this is kind of like a
smaller consumer version

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.770
of what they use in the competitions.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.610
I have no idea what
I've gotten myself into

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:35.610
with this unboxing
because this is something

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:36.600
that is programmable.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.700
You also have to put it
together, so this thing

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.530
comes in a bunch of different pieces.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:41.830
What I love about it is they're calling it

00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:43.580
an educational robot
so this isn't something

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:45.600
that just comes in the
box already put together.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.220
This is something that you put together,

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:48.970
that you learn how it works and using

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:51.280
Scratch and Python you can program it.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:52.940
You can write programs on your computer,

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.430
on mobile tablets, on Android, on iOS

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:57.640
and you can share them
instantly with your friends

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.720
or maybe even your not friends

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:02.350
because this thing is
made for competitions.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:04.420
So after this unboxing, I'm
going to put this together

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:05.320
and then I'm going to go meet up with

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:07.270
some friends who also have one.

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:10.350
Hmm, okay, this is substantial box.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:11.890
The box is actually not very heavy though

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:13.350
which is kinda cool.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:15.440
Oh my gosh.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:17.320
It's all in pieces.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:21.900
So, here's our instructions
and this is the one time

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:25.230
that you will see me place
these delicately off to the side

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:28.190
because I think that's
something I'm gonna need.

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:30.443
So this looks like it's
probably important.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.313
This is like a massive LEGO set.

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:38.083
There's a lot of pieces.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:42.470
Look at this lovely,
thoughtful little toolbox.

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:47.110
That's... that's something.

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:49.430
Oh my, this is gonna be really fun.

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:51.050
If you guys are new
here, one of the things

00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:54.150
that I love so much is, I love LEGO sets

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:56.230
and I used to love the Technic sets too

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:59.417
'cause you could actually
make things move and happen.

00:01:59.417 --> 00:02:00.310
I don't even think this
is going to be that

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:01.970
difficult to put together.

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:03.120
Am I missing something?

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:04.970
Oh, there's more.

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:07.680
I should probably just timelapse myself

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.150
putting this together 'cause I'm probably

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.410
going to be here for awhile.

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:12.040
Oh look, it's all together.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:14.220
Just kidding, this is
the one that they sent

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.340
